WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.109
Grab a refreshing tab Cola and a delicious prison burger because we have the 100th episode of American Horror Story.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:12.809
But before we get into our detailed breakdown. If you haven't checked out Castle Rock, I highly recommend it,

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:16.739
and yes I do breakdowns for it. Hashtag shameless self plug.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:22.500
We're in 1985, approximately a year after the events of camp redwoods second massacre.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:30.029
At the beautiful Hollywood premier motel, you know, it's a high-end establishment with the amount of prostitutes in the parking lot.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:36.359
Last episode, we left off with Ricky and Jingles heading off to Los Angeles to start a beautiful life together, terrorizing this City of Angels.

00:00:36.399 --> 00:00:40.319
But a year in things aren't going so well for our friend, Jingles.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.209
We'll get into that in a bit. A German woman on vacation with her husband, Horst and her two

00:00:45.399 --> 00:00:50.120
Children of the corn look-a-likes goes over to Ricky's room to tell him to turn it down.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:51.689
After all they have a busy day at Disneyland tomorrow

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:57.120
Also I love these tiny details, like the husband wearing a Hollywood souvenir shirt

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.300
So, you know, they're from out of town.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.669
Ricky opens his smoke-filled room eyeing the German woman, sexually.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:08.969
In the background, you can hear Billy Idol's Flesh for Fantasy, and we know how much Ricky loves Billy.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:16.769
He grabs the woman, but Jingles warns him to let her go and what is with that facial hair Jingles?

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:22.920
I mean come on. Jingles and Ricky have been here for a year and living with Ricky has gotten on Jingles nerves.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:27.629
He doesn't like the music and Ricky lives like an animal. Oh, and they're constantly killing.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:32.670
In fact Jingles says he's killed 11 and constantly haunted by the faces of his victims.

00:01:32.799 --> 00:01:36.659
He wants out but Ricky reminds him.

00:01:40.689 --> 00:01:42.898
If you remember at the end of last episode

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:49.319
Jingles was killed by Xavier and later given a second chance at life through the resurrected Ricky.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:53.849
He made a deal with the devil and although we never hear what this actual deal is

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:54.909
It's safe to assume

00:01:54.909 --> 00:01:58.828
It was life in exchange for eternal service to the Dark Lord

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.680
Service, which means killing and if Jingles breaks this deal, there will be hell to pay.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:04.800
Literally.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:05.980
Paranoid by Black Sabbath

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:11.340
plays as we see a short montage of Jingles watching, disapprovingly, as Ricky kills.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:18.820
At a nearby convenience store, Ricky goes in for a beer and Jingles changes the song to REO Speedwagon's Can't fight this feeling.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:23.980
Which has the lyric, "I've forgotten what I started fighting for". Our poor Jingles feels trapped

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:27.220
He's forgotten what he's fighting for. While looking at the paper

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:30.980
He sees that Ricky has been identified and is wanted for murder.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:34.980
Totally off-topic, but there's also an article talking about hurricane Elena

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:38.840
which was a real hurricane that pummeled, Florida around the same time.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:43.400
Jingles buys a copy of the paper and gives it to a woman who notices Ricky in the store.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:45.360
Soon a crowd of locals surround Ricky

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:51.220
calling him el matón, and if the high school Spanish, I mean Google Translate, is right, that means the killer*.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:57.480
He's chased down by the group and beaten to a pulp, as our tab drinking Jingles drives off into the distance.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:08.000
And we're back at Camp Redwood in the year, 1989, five years after the events of Episode five.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:12.529
We meet Dustin, the bird watcher, who stumbled across the camp in search for waterfowl.

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:16.729
He passes one of the cabins, which has since been abandoned and has graffiti exclaiming

00:03:16.799 --> 00:03:22.849
"Brooke wants your blood" a nod to how Brooke was framed by Margaret for the 1984 massacre.

00:03:22.849 --> 00:03:26.869
Home Sweet Home by Motley Crue plays when we see Montana sunbathing at the dock.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:31.459
We saw her last episode become one of the ghosts of Redwood unable to leave the grounds,

00:03:31.459 --> 00:03:36.589
but it seems as though she's made herself at home wanting to open our precious birdwatcher's fanny pack.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:40.160
I'm also curious if he takes a photo of her will she be visible in it?

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:44.569
Anyway, she tries to seduce him and he tells her he has a girlfriend. We'll get to her in a bit.

00:03:44.569 --> 00:03:47.598
But he succumbs to her charms and is brutally murdered by her

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:53.260
We then see Midge and the other two counselors from the original massacre commenting how unsophisticated

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:58.720
Montana is. Xavier calls them old-timers and proceeds to make out with Montana.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.940
Remember in episode 1, we learned that they used to date

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:04.280
so it looks like they've rekindled things.

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:06.780
The introduction of the original counselours here is interesting

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:13.700
because it may throw a wrench in the idea that; the only people who come back from the dead here are those that need to be redeemed

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:17.240
Margaret Booth is now on Lifestyles of the Rich and Famous

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:22.540
which was a real show in the 80s and 90s, which featured the extravagant lifestyles of wealthy

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:25.240
entertainers, athletes and business moguls.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:26.500
My god that hair!

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:30.880
She's used her money from her dead husband, the same one we heard about briefly in Episode 1

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:34.420
to buy properties with a dark history and turn them into attractions

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:37.900
Properties like serial killer John Wayne Gacy 's house

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:42.360
The Briarcliff Manor, which was the main focus of season two's Asylum,

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:44.000
Winchester Mystery House

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:47.630
which was the inspiration for the film, Winchester with Helen Mirren and

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:51.600
Spahn's Movie Ranch, where Charles Manson plotted his murders.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.520
And in an absolutely shocking twist, Trevor is still alive and

00:04:55.700 --> 00:05:00.900
married to Margaret, the same woman who stabbed him in Episode four and cut off his ear also.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.620
Look at that Sweet cell phone.

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:05.640
This relationship isn't what it's cracked up to be.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:09.020
Trevor's a coke and alcohol addict and Margaret has given up on God.

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:12.440
Through a flashback, we learned that Trevor is in it for the money.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:15.360
Rather than accuse Margaret for the murders and lose in court.

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:19.520
He might as well get something out of it and use Margaret as his sugar mama.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:25.070
But Margaret only agrees if he becomes her husband since you can't make your spouse testify against you.

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:30.004
But now Trevor feels trapped, just like Jingles, when Margaret's assistant Courtney comes in-

00:05:30.004 --> 00:05:32.660
this guy just plays the most ridiculous characters.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:38.980
He was in season three's coven or you might remember him as the eccentric medium Cricket in season six's Roanoke.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:42.600
He tells them that Brook has just lost her appeal and is set to be executed.

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:48.260
Going down what I believe to be death row, Brooke is confronted by Rickey who has since been captured.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:53.960
Xavier and Montana go through Dustin's campsite when Ray strolls in pissed that they've killed another innocent person.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:06:00.199
None of them know why they're stuck there and the old-timers seemed to be just as pissed as Ray, at the total disregard

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.920
Xavier and Montana have for other people's lives.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:06.020
They uncover a paper telling them of Brook's soon-to-be execution,

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:10.300
when Dustin's girlfriend arrives and Xavier makes quick work over her.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:13.560
Brooke is haunted by Ricky and the thoughts of her impending death with

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:16.370
The words "Your Final home" written in her cell.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:22.369
Ricky has somehow astral projected with the powers of Satan and makes Brooke a deal, his master believes

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:26.299
she has potential and asked her to join them to which she politely declines.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:30.470
We get another shot of Ricky with those black eyes

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:33.679
which we also saw possess Michael Langdon last season.

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:39.169
Margaret receives a report from Courtney that things are going well at their Lizzie Borden property, the woman who was

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:43.426
suspected of killing her father and stepmother with an axe in 1892.

00:06:43.426 --> 00:06:46.780
Courtney suggests they sell the business while their business is hot

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:53.200
but Margaret's greed is too much, which is a likely indicator that Margaret will die the season and lose everything.

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:55.220
Trevor shows them a newspaper.-- Damn

00:06:55.220 --> 00:07:02.239
There's a lot of newspapers in this episode-- that reports on the two found dead at Camp redwood and since they still own the property

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:03.560
They could be held liable,

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:05.360
but Margaret sees opportunity in this.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:08.420
We catch up to jingles who has started a new life in Alaska

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:14.180
with a woman named Lorraine, this actress also played Hayden McClaine's sister in season One's Murder House.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:17.989
Jingles apparently saved this woman's life. She used to be a prostitute,

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:20.569
so it's possible that they met at the Hollywood premiere.

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:24.829
They both now live a happy new life with Jingles working at Video Shack

00:07:24.829 --> 00:07:28.220
which is a throwback to video rental stores like Blockbuster.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:32.360
Here see his new alias Donald and some fun fake movie posters in the back.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:38.480
Donald might be up for a new position at the opening of a new Video Shack in Juneau, as Brett says

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:45.500
Margaret comes up with the brilliant idea to go back to camp redwood with a food and music

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:50.820
festival. People can actually stay in the cabins where the massacre happened, what could go wrong?

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:54.290
We also see Chet interacting with Montana here, pretty much

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:59.420
confirming that he did indeed die via drowning by Margaret and he wants his revenge.

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:02.180
Jingles watches the announcement of the festival, telling Lorraine

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:02.990
He's over it

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:04.990
He has a new life and he's free

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.220
But is he?

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:10.040
Meanwhile back in jail, Ricky is visited by an admirer simply known as Red

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:15.280
She tells him of Camp Redwood's Music Festival and we learn of Ricky's desire to be remembered.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:25.580
This was hinted at in previous episodes when he admired Jingles for being a legend.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:27.460
He wants to be one too.

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:29.629
Brooke enjoys her last meal of Snapple and

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:32.300
🤮 I've no idea what that is-

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:35.740
When Ricky offers her one last chance, a last chance she declines.

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:39.900
Ricky has made a pentagram to communicate with his master just like he did in

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:43.160
Episode four and like Michael Langdon did in season eight

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:49.980
he wants his master to give him another shot at immortality and, in return, will give him a torrent of fresh souls

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.820
Brooke pleads her innocence, spitting at Margaret behind the glass

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:56.689
She's locked in and given the lethal injection, dying two minutes later

00:08:56.690 --> 00:08:59.780
In fact, Margaret and Trevor are bored of the whole process

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:03.880
wishing that they would bring back something more exciting like the guillotine.

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:06.230
At the same time, Ricky has summoned the power of his master

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:09.060
which takes control of the guard who then sets him free.

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:12.769
Donald is chastised by a customer giving them rom-com instead of a horror

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:16.248
Which is probably gonna affect that big promotion he's supposed to get.

00:09:16.248 --> 00:09:19.040
When he arrives home, he finds Lorraine brutally murdered.

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:20.300
Luckily his little boy

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:25.480
Bobby is still alive with his sign written in blood saying "Satan will have his vengeance"

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:30.100
The back of it has a picture of the Camp Redwood Festival, leading us to believe it was Ricky who

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:32.090
had the same flyer with him in his cell

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:35.600
I also liked the use of the words gourmet  food and luxury tents

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:39.500
Which were the same words used to describe the disastrous Fyre Festival.

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:42.320
*subscribe to Think Story*

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:43.470
Also think it's a bit weird

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:50.000
If it was Ricky who left that note that he went all the way to Alaska then back to California, that's a really long trip.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:53.660
Jingles knew he would one day pay for not keeping his deal with the devil and

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:59.640
decides to end everything once and for all, by going back to Camp Redwood to finish Ricky once and for all.

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:04.700
He leaves his child with Lauren's sister,
saying his goodbyes, as if he's never going to come back.

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:13.860
He puts on his iconic,  Mr. Jingles

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:17.560
raincoat and makes sure to bring his keys with him.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:20.729
And in our final scene, Brooke is resuscitated by none other than Rita.

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:27.120
It's never really explained how Rita was able to bring her back, considering if Brooke was pronounced dead her heart would have stopped

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:31.010
So whatever Rita injected into her veins must have been pretty powerful.

00:10:31.010 --> 00:10:32.309
The last time we saw Rita,

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:35.960
she asked Jingles to kill her for what she had unleashed on the camp.

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:37.960
Rita is looking for redemption and from her

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:43.500
conversation with Jingles, knows Brooke is innocent and that Margaret is the real killer.

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:45.680
With Brooke wanting Margaret to pay and Rita in search of redemption,

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:50.280
the two will likely team up and head back to Camp Redwood.

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:52.290
With our characters all making their way back to camp,

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:56.820
It looks like the last few episodes will center around the final Camp Redwood massacre.

00:10:56.820 --> 00:10:59.600
I'm just hoping it's not as disastrous as Fyre Festival.

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:00.920
Thanks for watching everyone!

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:04.830
Please make sure to give the video a like and comment below with your theories and thoughts.

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:09.040
You can also reach me on Twitter @ThinkStoryYT.

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:10.949
Until next time remember- daddy loves you very much.

